-- EU AI Act: which text is in force, and when the scoped provisions apply.
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Articles 111 and 113 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, as enacted and as
-- amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. Each date is copied from the text.
-- Days are calendar days throughout; see NOTES.md, fork F7.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-domain`

§ `Dates`

-- The stable l4 has no YMD (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5), so this local
-- shim spells a date year-first.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD y m d MEANS Date d m y

§§ `Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Article 4: entry into force`

-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:8 | 24.7.2026
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:764 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the third day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- Published 24.7.2026; the third day following is 27 July 2026, the date the
-- same Regulation gives for new Article 113(d) and Article 97(2).
@ref Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Art 4; OJ L 24.7.2026 (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:8) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:764)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 entered into force` MEANS YMD 2026 7 27

-- Which vintage is the law on a given date: the text as enacted until the
-- amending Regulation entered into force, the amended text from then on.
@ref Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Art 4 (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:764)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `version of the Regulation`
`the version in force on` `the date` MEANS
    IF `the date` AT LEAST `the day Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 entered into force`
    THEN `as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744`
    ELSE `as enacted`

§§ `Article 113: entry into force and application`

-- src:2199 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
@ref Article 113, second paragraph (src:2199)
GIVETH A DATE
`the general date of application` MEANS YMD 2026 8 2

-- src:2202 | Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025;
@ref Article 113, third paragraph, point (a) (src:2202)
GIVETH A DATE
`Chapters I and II apply from` MEANS YMD 2025 2 2

-- src:2204 | Chapter III Section 4, Chapter V, Chapter VII and Chapter XII and Article 78 shall apply from 2 August 2025, with the exception of Article 101;
-- Chapter V holds Articles 51 to 56; Chapter XII holds Articles 99 to 101.
-- Article 101 is excepted, so it falls back to the general date.
@ref Article 113, third paragraph, point (b) (src:2204)
GIVETH A DATE
`Chapters V and XII apply from` MEANS YMD 2025 8 2

@ref Article 113, third paragraph, point (b), "with the exception of Article 101" (src:2204)
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 101 applies from` MEANS `the general date of application`

-- src:2206 | Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations in this Regulation shall apply from 2 August 2027.
@ref Article 113, third paragraph, point (c), as enacted (src:2206)
GIVETH A DATE
`as enacted, Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations apply from` MEANS YMD 2027 8 2

-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:622 | Chapter III, Sections 1, 2, and 3, with the exception of Article 6(5), shall apply from:
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:624 | 2 December 2027 as regards AI systems classified as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(2) and Annex III; and
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:626 | 2 August 2028 as regards AI systems classified as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(1) and Annex I;’
@ref Article 113, third paragraph, point (c), as replaced by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 Art 1(40)(b) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:622-626)
GIVETH A DATE
`as amended, Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to Annex III systems from` MEANS YMD 2027 12 2

@ref Article 113, third paragraph, point (c)(ii), as replaced (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:626)
GIVETH A DATE
`as amended, Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to Annex I systems from` MEANS YMD 2028 8 2

-- When Chapter III, Sections 1 to 3 (Articles 6 to 27, which include the
-- classification rules and Articles 16, 20 and 26) apply to a system.
-- As enacted: the general date, except that Article 6(1) systems wait for
-- point (c). As amended: point (c)(i) or (ii). No date for a system that is
-- not high-risk, or for a Section B product, which Article 2(2) leaves to
-- its own sectoral law (see aia-art73.l4).
@ref Article 113 (src:2199) (src:2206); as amended (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:622-626)
GIVEN v IS A `version of the Regulation`, r IS A `high-risk route`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply from` v r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `Article 6(2), listed in Annex III` THEN
        CONSIDER v
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN JUST `the general date of application`
        WHEN `as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744` THEN JUST `as amended, Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to Annex III systems from`
    WHEN `Article 6(1), product under Section A of Annex I` THEN
        CONSIDER v
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN JUST `as enacted, Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations apply from`
        WHEN `as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744` THEN JUST `as amended, Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to Annex I systems from`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- When Article 73 applies. Article 73 is in Chapter IX, not Chapter III.
-- As enacted, an Article 6(1) system's reporting duty is one of "the
-- corresponding obligations" of point (c), so it waits until 2 August 2027;
-- an Annex III system's applies from the general date.
-- As amended, point (c) names only Chapter III, Sections 1 to 3, and the words
-- "the corresponding obligations" are gone, so on the plain reading Article 73
-- applies from the general date for both routes. Article 111(2), as amended,
-- is what keeps it from reaching systems placed before the Chapter III date.
-- FORK F3 in NOTES.md.
@ref Article 113 (src:2199) (src:2206); as amended (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:622)
GIVEN v IS A `version of the Regulation`, r IS A `high-risk route`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date Article 73 applies from` v r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `Article 6(2), listed in Annex III` THEN JUST `the general date of application`
    WHEN `Article 6(1), product under Section A of Annex I` THEN
        CONSIDER v
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN JUST `as enacted, Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations apply from`
        WHEN `as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744` THEN JUST `the general date of application`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Article 111: systems and models already on the market`

-- src:2159 | 2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2026, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs. In any case, the providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations of this Regulation by 2 August 2030.
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:606 | ‘2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113, third paragraph, point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before the date of application of Chapter III referred to in Article 113, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs.
-- The cut-off date: 2 August 2026 as enacted; as amended, "the date of
-- application of Chapter III referred to in Article 113", which differs by
-- route. Article 111(1) (Annex X large-scale IT systems) is out of scope.
@ref Article 111(2) (src:2159); as replaced by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 Art 1(39)(a) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:606)
GIVEN v IS A `version of the Regulation`, r IS A `high-risk route`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the Article 111(2) cut-off date` v r MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `as enacted` THEN
        CONSIDER r
        WHEN `not a high-risk AI system` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST `the general date of application`
    WHEN `as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744` THEN `the date Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply from` v r

@ref Article 111(2), second sentence (src:2159)
GIVETH A DATE
`public-authority systems must comply by` MEANS YMD 2030 8 2

-- Whether Article 111(2) lets the Regulation reach my system on the date.
-- A system first placed on the market or put into service on or after the
-- cut-off is not caught by Article 111(2) at all. One placed before it is
-- reached only once its design changes significantly on or after the cut-off,
-- or, if it is intended for public authorities, from 2 August 2030.
-- "Shall take the necessary steps to comply ... by 2 August 2030" is read as
-- the date from which the obligations bind: FORK F4 in NOTES.md.
@ref Article 111(2) (src:2159); as amended (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:606)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 111(2) lets the Regulation reach my system on` `the date` v s MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Article 111(2) cut-off date` v (s's `the route by which the system is high-risk`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST cutoff THEN
            s's `the date the system was first placed on the market or put into service` AT LEAST cutoff
        OR  `its design changed significantly on or after` cutoff `and by` `the date` s
        OR  (    s's `the system is intended to be used by public authorities`
             AND `the date` AT LEAST `public-authority systems must comply by`)

GIVEN cutoff IS A DATE, `the date` IS A DATE, s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`its design changed significantly on or after` cutoff `and by` `the date` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `the date of the latest significant change to its design, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST changed THEN changed AT LEAST cutoff AND changed AT MOST `the date`

-- src:2160 | 3. Providers of general-purpose AI models that have been placed on the market before 2 August 2025 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2027.
-- Read as: for a model placed before 2 August 2025, the Chapter V
-- obligations bind from 2 August 2027 (FORK F4 in NOTES.md); for any other
-- model, from the date Chapter V applies.
@ref Article 111(3) (src:2160); Article 113(b) (src:2204)
GIVEN m IS A `model facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the Chapter V obligations bind me for this model` m MEANS
    IF m's `the date the model was first placed on the market` LESS THAN `Chapters V and XII apply from`
    THEN YMD 2027 8 2
    ELSE `Chapters V and XII apply from`
